 "coords": "Same grid / frame numbers / origin as spr_player (and spr_player_autoaim): play the overlay on the body's CURRENT frame index, same x / y / flipX / rotation.  Draw order: body -> helmet -> weapon arm layer -> shoulder (the pad sits over the arm-layer pivot, so the arm always comes out from under it).  Every body sheet has its own pair named <body key>_armor_<layer> (spr_player, spr_player_autoaim, and the melee swing sheets spr_player_melee / spr_player_melee_<id> - build_armor_melee.py, player_melee_armor.json); a body texture without a pair hides the overlays.",
 "unlock": "training line 'armor': Lv5 shoulder, Lv15 helmet (player_v01.json milestones armor.5 / armor.15, stat armorLook 1 / 2)",
 "lighting": {
  "rim": "<layer>_rim.png: rows L / R / T (frame index = row * 55 + frame), already lightened like the runtime bake (rim.ts LIGHTEN .55); exposure measured against the body + armour composite, so edges lying inside the body silhouette get no rim.  The engine registers it as <key>__rim with frames 'L:<i>' 'R:<i>' 'T:<i>'.",
  "normal": "<layer>_n.png: player_n.png convention (bevel per part, pieces are their own parts); not in the manifest.",
  "emit": "none: the helmet overlay is transparent on the head-lamp pixels, spr_player_emit / points.lamp unchanged."
 },
